<title>MEXICO: Mexico says to centralise budget spending.</title>
<headline>Mexico says to centralise budget spending.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico plans to centralise control over its budget spending, deputy Finance Minister Martin Werner said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Werner told reporters the Finance Ministry will control spending at different government ministries through a computer system in order to ensure the money is spent efficiently.</p>
<p>Werner said the reform was part of the government's National Plan for Financing Development, unveiled by President Ernesto Zedillo on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He had no futher details on how the plan would work.</p>
<p>(--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9565)</p>
